# The build context is what the Dockerfile copies and nothing else (an allowlist): the
# package, its metadata and the lockfile. Keys (.env), data, the evaluation, the docs, the
# site and the tests stay out, so that a build of a checkout never carries a key or a
# document into an image (tests/test_container.py checks the list against the Dockerfile).
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.pyc
